invReduce -- compute normal form modulo involutive basis by involutive reduction
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (r,c) = invReduce(p,J)
  * Inputs:
      * p, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the columns are to be reduced
        modulo J
      * J, an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis: InvolutiveBasis,
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the normal form of (the
        columns of) p modulo J
      * c, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the reduction coefficients
  * Consequences:
      * the columns of r are in normal form modulo J, and p = r + J#0 * c,
        where * is matrix multiplication

Description
===========

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                             |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = matrix {{x+y+z, x*y+y*z+z*x, x*y*z-1}};|
|                                                |
|             1      3                           |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                            |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = janetBasis M;                          |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : p = matrix {{y,y^2,y^3}}                   |
|                                                |
|o4 = | y y2 y3 |                                |
|                                                |
|             1      3                           |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                            |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : invReduce(p,J)                             |
|                                                |
|o5 = (| y -yz-z2 1 |, | 0 0 0   |)              |
|                      | 0 1 y-z |               |
|                      | 0 0 1   |               |
|                      | 0 0 0   |               |
|                                                |
|o5 : Sequence                                   |
+------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note janetBasis: janetBasis, -- compute Janet basis for an ideal or a
    submodule of a free module
  * *note invSyzygies: invSyzygies, -- compute involutive basis of syzygies

Ways to use invReduce:
======================

  * "invReduce(Matrix,InvolutiveBasis)"
  * "invReduce(RingElement,InvolutiveBasis)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note invReduce: invReduce, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

