invSyzygies -- compute involutive basis of syzygies
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        invSyzygies J
  * Inputs:
      * J, an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis: InvolutiveBasis,
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis: InvolutiveBasis,, an
        involutive basis for the syzygies of J

Description
===========

+-----------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];    |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x,y,z); |
|                       |
|o2 : Ideal of R        |
+-----------------------+
|i3 : J = janetBasis I  |
|                       |
|     +-+---------+     |
|o3 = |z|{z}      |     |
|     +-+---------+     |
|     |y|{z, y}   |     |
|     +-+---------+     |
|     |x|{z, y, x}|     |
|     +-+---------+     |
|                       |
|o3 : InvolutiveBasis   |
+-----------------------+
|i4 : invSyzygies J     |
|                       |
|     +------+---------+|
|o4 = ||  x ||{z, y, x}||
|     ||  0 ||         ||
|     || -z ||         ||
|     +------+---------+|
|     ||  y ||{z, y}   ||
|     || -z ||         ||
|     ||  0 ||         ||
|     +------+---------+|
|     ||  0 ||{z, y, x}||
|     ||  x ||         ||
|     || -y ||         ||
|     +------+---------+|
|                       |
|o4 : InvolutiveBasis   |
+-----------------------+

Caveat
======

cannot be iterated because *note schreyerOrder: (Macaulay2Doc)schreyerOrder, is
not used; call *note janetResolution: janetResolution, instead

See also
========

  * *note janetBasis: janetBasis, -- compute Janet basis for an ideal or a
    submodule of a free module
  * *note janetResolution: janetResolution, -- construct a free resolution for
    a given ideal or module using Janet bases

Ways to use invSyzygies:
========================

  * "invSyzygies(InvolutiveBasis)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note invSyzygies: invSyzygies, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

