isPommaretBasis -- check whether or not a given Janet basis is also a Pommaret basis
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        P = isPommaretBasis J
  * Inputs:
      * J, an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis: InvolutiveBasis,, a
        Janet basis as returned by *note janetBasis: janetBasis,
  * Outputs:
      * P, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, the result equals
        true if and only if J is a Pommaret basis

Description
===========

+------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];       |
+------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^3,y^2);|
|                        |
|o2 : Ideal of R         |
+------------------------+
|i3 : J = janetBasis I   |
|                        |
|     +----+------+      |
|     | 2  |      |      |
|o3 = |y   |{y}   |      |
|     +----+------+      |
|     |   2|      |      |
|     |x*y |{y}   |      |
|     +----+------+      |
|     | 3  |      |      |
|     |x   |{y, x}|      |
|     +----+------+      |
|     | 2 2|      |      |
|     |x y |{y}   |      |
|     +----+------+      |
|                        |
|o3 : InvolutiveBasis    |
+------------------------+
|i4 : isPommaretBasis J  |
|                        |
|o4 = true               |
+------------------------+
+------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x,y];       |
+------------------------+
|i6 : I = ideal(x*y,y^2);|
|                        |
|o6 : Ideal of R         |
+------------------------+
|i7 : J = janetBasis I   |
|                        |
|     +---+------+       |
|     | 2 |      |       |
|o7 = |y  |{y}   |       |
|     +---+------+       |
|     |x*y|{y, x}|       |
|     +---+------+       |
|                        |
|o7 : InvolutiveBasis    |
+------------------------+
|i8 : isPommaretBasis J  |
|                        |
|o8 = false              |
+------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note janetBasis: janetBasis, -- compute Janet basis for an ideal or a
    submodule of a free module
  * *note basisElements: basisElements, -- extract the matrix of generators
    from an involutive basis or factor module basis
  * *note multVar: multVar, -- extract the sets of multiplicative variables for
    each generator (in several contexts)
  * *note janetMultVar: janetMultVar, -- return table of multiplicative
    variables for given module elements as determined by Janet division
  * *note pommaretMultVar: pommaretMultVar, -- return table of multiplicative
    variables for given module elements as determined by Pommaret division

Ways to use isPommaretBasis:
============================

  * "isPommaretBasis(InvolutiveBasis)"

