janetBasis -- compute Janet basis for an ideal or a submodule of a free module
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        J = janetBasis M or J = janetBasis(C,n)
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis: InvolutiveBasis,
      * M, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
      * M, a *note Gröbner basis: (Macaulay2Doc)GroebnerBasis,
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * J, an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis: InvolutiveBasis,

Description
===========

If the argument for janetBasis is a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, or an
*note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, or a *note Gröbner basis:
(Macaulay2Doc)GroebnerBasis,, then J is a Janet basis for (the module generated
by) M.

If the arguments for janetBasis are a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex, and an
*note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, where C is the result of either *note
janetResolution: janetResolution, or *note freeResolution:
(Complexes)freeResolution, called with the optional argument 'Strategy =>
Involutive', then J is the Janet basis extracted from the n-th differential of
C.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                           |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^3,y^2);                    |
|                                            |
|o2 : Ideal of R                             |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = janetBasis I;                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : basisElements J                        |
|                                            |
|o4 = | y2 xy2 x3 x2y2 |                     |
|                                            |
|             1      4                       |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : multVar J                              |
|                                            |
|o5 = {set {y}, set {y}, set {y, x}, set {y}}|
|                                            |
|o5 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : M = matrix {{x*y-y^3, x*y^2, x*y-x}, {x, y^2, x}};                      |
|                                                                             |
|             2      3                                                        |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : J = janetBasis M;                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : basisElements J                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = | y3-x xy-x x2y-x2 x3 -x      x2 -x2        0         |                 |
|     | 0    x    x2     x2 xy-y2+x y3 x2y-xy2+x2 x3+2x2+y2 |                 |
|                                                                             |
|             2      8                                                        |
|o9 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : multVar J                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = {set {y}, set {y}, set {y}, set {y, x}, set {y}, set {y}, set {y}, set |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      {y, x}}                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : I = ideal(x,y,z);                            |
|                                                   |
|o12 : Ideal of R                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : C = freeResolution(I, Strategy => Involutive)|
|                                                   |
|       1      3      3      1                      |
|o13 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0                |
|                                                   |
|      0      1      2      3      4                |
|                                                   |
|o13 : Complex                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : janetBasis(C, 2)                             |
|                                                   |
|      +------+---------+                           |
|o14 = || -y ||{z, y, x}|                           |
|      ||  x ||         |                           |
|      ||  0 ||         |                           |
|      +------+---------+                           |
|      || -z ||{z, y, x}|                           |
|      ||  0 ||         |                           |
|      ||  x ||         |                           |
|      +------+---------+                           |
|      ||  0 ||{z, y}   |                           |
|      || -z ||         |                           |
|      ||  y ||         |                           |
|      +------+---------+                           |
|                                                   |
|o14 : InvolutiveBasis                              |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note janetMultVar: janetMultVar, -- return table of multiplicative
    variables for given module elements as determined by Janet division
  * *note pommaretMultVar: pommaretMultVar, -- return table of multiplicative
    variables for given module elements as determined by Pommaret division
  * *note isPommaretBasis: isPommaretBasis, -- check whether or not a given
    Janet basis is also a Pommaret basis
  * *note invReduce: invReduce, -- compute normal form modulo involutive basis
    by involutive reduction
  * *note invSyzygies: invSyzygies, -- compute involutive basis of syzygies
  * *note janetResolution: janetResolution, -- construct a free resolution for
    a given ideal or module using Janet bases

Ways to use janetBasis:
=======================

  * "janetBasis(Complex,ZZ)"
  * "janetBasis(GroebnerBasis)"
  * "janetBasis(Ideal)"
  * "janetBasis(Matrix)"
  * janetBasis(Module) (missing documentation)

