janetResolution -- construct a free resolution for a given ideal or module using Janet bases
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = janetResolution M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, or an *note ideal:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, or a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a (non-minimal) free
        resolution of (the module generated by) M

Description
===========

The computed Janet basis for each homological degree can be extracted with
*note janetBasis: janetBasis,.

The sets of multiplicative variables can also be extracted from the Janet basis
in each homological degree with *note multVar: multVar,.

Note that janetResolution can be combined with *note freeResolution:
(Complexes)freeResolution,: when providing the option 'Strategy => Involutive'
to *note freeResolution: (Complexes)freeResolution,, janetResolution constructs
the resolution.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                            |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = matrix {{x,y,z}};                     |
|                                               |
|             1      3                          |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = janetResolution M                     |
|                                               |
|      1      3      3      1                   |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0             |
|                                               |
|     0      1      2      3      4             |
|                                               |
|o3 : Complex                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : janetBasis(C, 2)                          |
|                                               |
|     +------+---------+                        |
|o4 = || -y ||{z, y, x}|                        |
|     ||  x ||         |                        |
|     ||  0 ||         |                        |
|     +------+---------+                        |
|     || -z ||{z, y, x}|                        |
|     ||  0 ||         |                        |
|     ||  x ||         |                        |
|     +------+---------+                        |
|     ||  0 ||{z, y}   |                        |
|     || -z ||         |                        |
|     ||  y ||         |                        |
|     +------+---------+                        |
|                                               |
|o4 : InvolutiveBasis                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : multVar(C, 2)                             |
|                                               |
|o5 = {set {z, y, x}, set {z, y, x}, set {z, y}}|
|                                               |
|o5 : List                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+
+----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                           |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : I = ideal(x,y,z);                        |
|                                              |
|o7 : Ideal of R                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : freeResolution(I, Strategy => Involutive)|
|                                              |
|      1      3      3      1                  |
|o8 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0            |
|                                              |
|     0      1      2      3      4            |
|                                              |
|o8 : Complex                                  |
+----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note janetBasis: janetBasis, -- compute Janet basis for an ideal or a
    submodule of a free module
  * *note multVar: multVar, -- extract the sets of multiplicative variables for
    each generator (in several contexts)
  * *note invSyzygies: invSyzygies, -- compute involutive basis of syzygies

