File: InvolutiveBases.info, Node: multVar, Next: multVars, Prev: janetResolution, Up: Top

multVar -- extract the sets of multiplicative variables for each generator (in several contexts)
************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        m = multVar(J) or m = multVar(C,n) or m = multVar(F)
  * Inputs:
      * J, an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis: InvolutiveBasis,
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * F, an instance of the type *note FactorModuleBasis: FactorModuleBasis,
  * Outputs:
      * m, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of sets of variables of the
        polynomial ring

Description
===========

If the argument of multVar is an instance of the type *note InvolutiveBasis:
InvolutiveBasis,, then the i-th set in m consists of the multiplicative
variables for the i-th generator in J.

If the arguments of multVar are a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex, and an
*note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, where C is the result of either *note
janetResolution: janetResolution, or *note freeResolution:
(Complexes)freeResolution, called with the optional argument 'Strategy =>
Involutive', then the i-th set in m consists of the multiplicative variables
for the i-th generator in the n-th differential of C.

If the argument of multVar is an instance of the type *note FactorModuleBasis:
FactorModuleBasis,, then the i-th set in m consists of the multiplicative
variables for the i-th monomial cone in F.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                           |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^3,y^2);                    |
|                                            |
|o2 : Ideal of R                             |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = janetBasis I;                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : multVar J                              |
|                                            |
|o4 = {set {y}, set {y}, set {y, x}, set {y}}|
|                                            |
|o4 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = ideal(x,y,z);                            |
|                                                  |
|o6 : Ideal of R                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : C = freeResolution(I, Strategy => Involutive)|
|                                                  |
|      1      3      3      1                      |
|o7 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0                |
|                                                  |
|     0      1      2      3      4                |
|                                                  |
|o7 : Complex                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : multVar(C, 2)                                |
|                                                  |
|o8 = {set {z, y, x}, set {z, y, x}, set {z, y}}   |
|                                                  |
|o8 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------+
|i9 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i10 : M = matrix {{x*y,x^3*z}};              |
|                                             |
|              1      2                       |
|o10 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i11 : J = janetBasis M                       |
|                                             |
|      +---+---------+                        |
|o11 = |x*y|{z, y}   |                        |
|      +---+---------+                        |
|      | 2 |         |                        |
|      |x y|{z, y}   |                        |
|      +---+---------+                        |
|      | 3 |         |                        |
|      |x z|{z, x}   |                        |
|      +---+---------+                        |
|      | 3 |         |                        |
|      |x y|{z, y, x}|                        |
|      +---+---------+                        |
|                                             |
|o11 : InvolutiveBasis                        |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i12 : F = factorModuleBasis J                |
|                                             |
|      +--+------+                            |
|o12 = |1 |{z, y}|                            |
|      +--+------+                            |
|      |x |{z}   |                            |
|      +--+------+                            |
|      | 2|      |                            |
|      |x |{z}   |                            |
|      +--+------+                            |
|      | 3|      |                            |
|      |x |{x}   |                            |
|      +--+------+                            |
|                                             |
|o12 : FactorModuleBasis                      |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i13 : basisElements F                        |
|                                             |
|o13 = | 1 x x2 x3 |                          |
|                                             |
|              1      4                       |
|o13 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i14 : multVar F                              |
|                                             |
|o14 = {set {z, y}, set {z}, set {z}, set {x}}|
|                                             |
|o14 : List                                   |
+---------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note janetBasis: janetBasis, -- compute Janet basis for an ideal or a
    submodule of a free module
  * *note janetMultVar: janetMultVar, -- return table of multiplicative
    variables for given module elements as determined by Janet division
  * *note pommaretMultVar: pommaretMultVar, -- return table of multiplicative
    variables for given module elements as determined by Pommaret division
  * *note basisElements: basisElements, -- extract the matrix of generators
    from an involutive basis or factor module basis
  * *note janetResolution: janetResolution, -- construct a free resolution for
    a given ideal or module using Janet bases
